tober 22 at 10:45PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall\ncontinues.\n\n* WHERE...West Central Montezuma County in southwestern Colorado...\nSoutheastern San Juan County in southeastern Utah...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1045 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Streams\ncontinue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier rainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 837 PM MDT, River gages indicate high flow through McElmo\nCanyon and water levels continue to rise. Flooding is ongoing or\nexpected to begin shortly in the warned area.\n- This includes but is not limited to the following streams\nanddrainages...\nFlorida River, Spring Creek, Ute Creek, Salt Creek and Dry Creek.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nLow-lying areas along McElmo Creek between Cortez and Aneth.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-22T22:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Montezuma, CO; San Juan, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1616bea532703e8b3755c48a98fe0adbdb19a4d.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.d1616bea532703e8b3755c48a98fe0adbdb19a4d.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 1:49PM MDT until October 23 at 12:00PM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, Animas River Basin, Four Corners/Upper Dolores River, San\nJuan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains and Utah,\nincluding the following areas, Arches/Grand Flat,\nCanyonlands/Natural Bridges, La Sal and Abajo Mountains and\nSoutheast Utah.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, recent burn scars and other low-lying and\nflood-prone locations. Low-water crossings may be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is likely with additional rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms expected through Thursday night. The potential for\nflooding impacts continues into Friday.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T00:06:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 230006 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 606 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Widespread rain continues through early Friday. - Flooding/Flash Flooding is likely across portions of southwest Colorado and southeast Utah. - Modeled responses suggest several rivers reaching bankfull or higher at river forecast points across southwest C","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-23T01:16:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-231000- Little Snake Forecast Area- 716 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"mnc01","station_name":"Mancos","distance_km":18.6,"soil_temp_5cm_